          "kicker": "Squad selection",
          "heading": "Jake White brings back Nathan Hughes and names four uncapped Fiji players",
          "body": "Former England international Nathan Hughes is back in the Fiji frame, drafted into a 35-man Nations Championship squad that includes three other uncapped players: Peniami Narisia, Marika Parker and Setareki Bituniyata. Hughes won 22 caps for England between 2016 and 2019, the last in the 38-38 draw with Scotland in the 2019 Six Nations. The squad follows the 34-28 win over Japan and faces France, Ireland and Italy, as Jake White looks to lift Fiji off the bottom of the Southern Hemisphere pool."
